      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to express it in the form \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\), where \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers. By expanding the product, we get:\n\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nThis must equal the original quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\). Therefore, we can equate the coefficients:\n\n\\[\np + q = b \\quad \\text{and} \\quad pq = 2008\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the factor pairs of 2008 and determine the pair that gives the smallest positive value for \\( b = p + q \\). Let's list the factor pairs of 2008:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&1 \\cdot 2008, \\\\\n&2 \\cdot 1004, \\\\\n&4 \\cdot 502, \\\\\n&8 \\cdot 251.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nFor each pair, we calculate \\( b = p + q \\):\n\n1. For the pair \\( (1, 2008) \\):\n   \\[\n   b = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n   \\]\n\n2. For the pair \\( (2, 1004) \\):\n   \\[\n   b = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n   \\]\n\n3. For the pair \\( (4, 502) \\):\n   \\[\n   b = 4 + 502 = 506\n   \\]\n\n4. For the pair \\( (8, 251) \\):\n   \\[\n   b = 8 + 251 = 259\n   \\]\n\nAmong these values, the smallest positive integer for \\( b \\) is 259. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
